[list]
[*]Works with Dubs Rimatomics. Put a stand in a reactor hall, stock it with rad suits, and whoever loads or unloads fuel changes into them before touching a rod, then changes back when they move on to something else. Nothing to configure.
[*]Reactor halls needed a new way of being recognised. Rimatomics gives none of its buildings a room role, so the game scores a reactor hall exactly the way it scores an empty box, and a stand keyed to the room's role had nothing to go on. A stand now also reads what is standing in the room with it, which is how it finds the reactor cores, the plutonium processor and the spent fuel pool. This is the first time a stand can turn itself on without a room role, and it is the part of this release most worth telling you about.
[*]Nuclear rooms turn themselves on for research as well as for fuel work. The steps you run at a research reactor or a plutonium processor are the ones that can spring a radiation leak, with your researcher standing at the thing when it does, so a stand in those rooms now dresses them for it without you ticking anything. A spent fuel pool arms for fuel work alone, and a weapons bench for research alone, because that is what happens in each.
[*]The nuclear machining table and the Rimatomics research bench now make their rooms count as a workshop and a laboratory, which is what the same two benches from any other mod already did. A stand in either room arms itself as you would expect.
[*]The nuclear work type is listed as "Nuclear loading". It was always in the list, but under the name "Loading", because Rimatomics calls it Nuclear in the work tab and Loading in the field a list like this one reads from. The row worked; it was just under a name nobody hunting for "Nuclear" would find, which is easy to read as the mod not supporting Rimatomics at all.
[*]Fixed: fetching fuel rods looked in the wrong room. Those jobs name the reactor core as the destination and the rod as the thing being carried, and the colonist walks to the rod first, so a stand beside the storage pool is the one that should fire. It was looking beside the core instead, and a colonist would carry a rod the length of the base with no suit on. Stands beside the pool now count.
[*]Fetching chemfuel for the plutonium processor does not trigger a change, on purpose. Chemfuel is inert, and it lives wherever your colony stores chemfuel rather than beside a reactor, so treating that haul as nuclear work meant a trip to a wardrobe before a walk across the map, or two of them if the colonist was already suited. They keep whatever they are wearing and get on with it. Carrying the spent rods themselves still changes them, at the rods.
[*]Working the reactor console is deliberately not covered. It is a right click order rather than a job, with no work type behind it, and a shift change never interrupts an order you gave. In practice whoever loaded the fuel is already wearing the suit when you send them to the console.
[*]Nothing changes for a game without Dubs Rimatomics, and no setting moved.
[/list]
